@* The band a reference sheet ends with when it was opened from a picker: the way back to the
   list, and — pushed to the far end — whatever this sheet offers instead of it, a button that
   takes the subject or a line saying the pick is made above.

   The four sheets that have one wrote it out identically, down to the ml-auto on the trailing
   half, which is the sort of thing that stays identical right up until it doesn't. *@

<div class="sheet-foot">
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" @onclick="OnBack">
        <Icon Name="arrow-left" Class="w-3.5 h-3.5"/> Back to @BackLabel
    </button>
    @if (ChildContent is not null)
    {
        <div class="ml-auto">@ChildContent</div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>What the sheet came from, in the plural — "spirits", "adversaries".</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string BackLabel { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback OnBack { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The far end of the band: the action that takes this subject, or the note that
    /// says the pick is one of the choices above.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
